{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Path"]]},"sections":[],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Instance Method","externalID":"s:11OpenSwiftUI4PathV10addEllipse2in9transformy0A7Spatial6Rect3DV_AG17AffineTransform3DVtF","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"OpenSwiftUI"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"addEllipse"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"in"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Rect3D","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSpatial6Rect3DV"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"transform"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"AffineTransform3D","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSpatial17AffineTransform3DV"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"title":"addEllipse(in:transform:)","symbolKind":"method"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"mutating"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"addEllipse"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"in"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"internalParam","text":"rect"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Rect3D","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSpatial6Rect3DV"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"transform"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"AffineTransform3D","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSpatial17AffineTransform3DV"},{"text":" = .identity)","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"parameters":[{"name":"rect","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A rectangle that defines the area for the ellipse to fit in."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An affine transform to apply to the ellipse before adding to the path. Defaults to the identity transform if not specified."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"transform"}],"kind":"parameters"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The ellipse is approximated by a sequence of Bézier curves.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Its center is the midpoint of the rectangle defined by the rect parameter.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"If the rectangle is square, then the ellipse is circular with a radius equal to one-half the width (or height) of the rectangle.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"If the rect parameter specifies a rectangular shape, then the major and minor axes of the ellipse are defined by the width and height of the rectangle.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The ellipse forms a complete subpath of the path— that is, the ellipse drawing starts with a move-to operation and ends with a close-subpath operation, with all moves oriented in the clockwise direction.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/openswiftui\/path\/addellipse(in:transform:)"]}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Adds an ellipse that fits inside the specified rectangle to the path."}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Path\/addEllipse(in:transform:)"},"references":{"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/Path/addEllipse(in:transform:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui\/path\/addellipse(in:transform:)","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"addEllipse"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"in"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSpatia